IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS

A. Layout
- Add a compact dedicated dashboard component, preferably:
  frontend/src/components/dashboard/DashboardInsightsCarousel.jsx
  (Use the project's existing language/type conventions if a TypeScript equivalent is clearly more appropriate.)
- Place it immediately below Total Revenue in the left-side dashboard layout. Inspect the full grid before editing; do not guess the insertion point.
- Keep the three existing KPI cards and their current right-column arrangement intact.
- Preserve responsive behavior: on narrow screens, sections should stack naturally with no fixed-height whitespace or horizontal overflow.
- Reuse existing design tokens, Card primitives, typography, dark-mode styles, and Heroicons. Avoid a new visual system, arbitrary hard-coded colors, glass effects, or decorative filler.

B. Data adapter
- Adapt the existing insights object locally. Expected broad fields include:
  insights.alerts[]
  insights.recommendations[]
  insights.trends[]
- Inspect the actual backend response/types before relying on any field.
- Normalize eligible records into a safe display model with stable keys, category, title, message, priority/severity, and insight kind.
- Validate object/string/array shapes and safely handle missing or malformed values.
- Do not invent statistics, growth percentages, stock counts, money values, or business claims.
- Do not turn a trend point into a fabricated interpretation. Only show a trend if its existing data supports the wording; otherwise omit it from the carousel.
- Avoid duplicate entries where feasible.
- Use useful real content from alerts/recommendations. If the eligible pool is empty, show a calm empty state; never generate filler insights.
- Do not expose raw exception details or sensitive tenant data.

C. Carousel behavior
- Rotate every 30,000 ms only when there are at least two eligible insights.
- Rotation must be local state only and must not trigger API/AI/database requests.
- Provide Previous/Next controls and pagination indicators/buttons with accessible names.
- Manual navigation must work and wrap around correctly.
- Pause automatic rotation while the pointer is over the carousel or keyboard focus is inside it; resume when the pointer/focus leaves.
- Clear timers on unmount and recreate them safely when the eligible item count or pause state changes.
- Reset/clamp the active index safely when the insight list changes or shrinks (for example after refresh or shop switch).
- Respect reduced-motion preferences if any transition animation is introduced. Keep transitions subtle; avoid unnecessary animation dependencies.
- Use semantic buttons, visible keyboard focus, suitable ARIA labels, and no keyboard traps.
- Do not announce every automatic slide through a noisy aria-live region.
- The carousel is intentionally pure-carousel behavior. Do not pin an item or change rotation based on priority. Existing dashboard stock alerts remain accessible in their existing section.

D. Loading, empty, and failure states
- Use the existing dashboard insights loading lifecycle.
- Show a compact skeleton/loading state while insights are loading.
- Show a useful, non-alarming empty state if no valid insights exist.
- If insight fetching fails, do not crash the dashboard. Follow existing app error conventions and preserve any available retry behavior.
- Do not add another fetch, polling interval, or duplicated insights state.
- When Refresh is used, the carousel should reflect the refreshed insights automatically.

E. Navigation
- Include a “View all” action that navigates to the existing AI insights route using the established navigation conventions (expected route: /ai/insights; verify in code).
- Do not invent action destinations or non-existent buttons.

F. Security and scope
- Reuse existing authorized dashboard data; do not request arbitrary shop IDs or add a new API.
- Preserve active-shop/tenant scoping and existing permissions.
- Never bypass RBAC or alter backend authorization.
- No backend files should change for this task unless you stop and explain why a genuine dependency requires it.

